  "summary": "Postinstall executes remote shell script from third-party GitHub repo",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js runs `execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...')` as part of the package's dependency setup, fetching and executing a shell script from a mutable branch of an unrelated GitHub repository (`rtk-ai/rtk`) that does not match the package publisher (`@leejungkiin/awkit`). The script also reaches `https://www.rtk-ai.app`, uses `os.homedir()`, `process.platform`, and `child_process` to platform-branch and stage the fetched content. Because the fetch targets a mutable `refs/heads/master` reference on a third-party repo with no pinning, hash, or signature verification, the installer executes whatever code that repository serves at install time.",
